		)
		(uuid "9f760eb0-9752-4c9f-85c9-4444ccf33b7b")
	)
	(text "D4/D5/D6: MCP73871 STAT1/LBO, STAT2, ~PG are open-drain (pseudo open-drain for PG): they sink\nonly, ISINK max 35mA, VOL 0.4V typ @4mA (DS20002090E sec 3.10-3.12, DC table \"Status Indicators\").\nTruth table (Table 5-1): D4 only = charging; D5 only = charged; D4+D5 = temp/timer fault;\nD4 alone with D6 off = low battery on battery power (LBO -- only if the ordered MCP73871 variant\nhas LBO enabled; the orderable suffix is not chosen yet); D6 = adapter present.\nIf any of these is also read by a host GPIO, the GPIO sees ~VSYS - VF (up to ~3.2V+) when the\noutput is off -- add a series R / divider on the connectivity side, do not tap the LED node raw."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 162.56 50.8 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.1 1.1)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "a386b9a7-b206-4fd8-af4f-8f19ffa39a44")
	)
	(text "D7/D400/D401: GPIO -> R -> LED -> GND, so an unpowered MCU cannot be back-fed through an\nLED from +3V3. Low-current AlGaInP parts (specified at IF = 2mA) chosen so ~1mA is visible\nand standard GPIO drive is enough. Resistors computed from the Kingbright datasheet VF at\nthe actual drive rail -- replaces the old indicative 1k (decisions.md Open item).\nNOT VERIFIED: nRF9151 GPIO VOH / drive strength and VIO level (PS not available offline);\nKingbright cathode mark vs KiCad LED_0805 pad 1 = K -- check the drawing at footprint time."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 162.56 116.84 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.1 1.1)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "b2af05d1-f6dd-42d4-8d6d-d77ee9bc7b6f")
	)
	(text "MCP73871 charger status (power_bms) -- open-drain sinks, LED from the pin's legal rail"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 40.64 54.61 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.5 1.5)
				(bold yes)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "daa2143e-1fd0-462c-972a-76c4a64fb84a")
	)
	(text "Host / radio LEDs -- GPIO sources, active HIGH, <=1.5 mA"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 40.64 100.33 0)
		(effects
